#{[{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097588} :activity/id #uuid "85353624-7ac2-52d1-8562-1afe91b8759a" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048976 :topic/id #uuid "d0827a60-1270-5e75-a5db-1a9836dc00b1" :topic/math-academy-id 1079} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097588 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097791 :tutorial/content "For a particle with position $x(t)$, the **average velocity** of the particle over the time interval $[a,b]$ is given by the average rate of change of position:\n\n$$\nv_{\\textrm{avg}} = \\dfrac{\\Delta x}{\\Delta t} = \\dfrac{x(b) - x(a)}{b-a}\n$$\n\nSimilarly, the **average acceleration** of a particle with velocity $v(t)$ over the time interval $[a,b]$ is given by the average rate of change of velocity:\n\n$$\na_{\\textrm{avg}} = \\dfrac{\\Delta v}{\\Delta t} = \\dfrac{v(b) - v(a)}{b-a}\n$$\n\nTo demonstrate, suppose that a particle moves along a straight line, and its position (in meters) relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by the function\n\n$$\nx(t) = 2t^3\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nt \\geq 0\n$$\n\nis the time measured in seconds. The average velocity of the particle over the time interval $[0,1]$ is\n\n$$\nv_{avg} = \\frac{Δx}{Δt} = (x(1) - x(0))/(1 - 0) = (2(1)^{3} - 2(0)^{3})/(1 - 0) = 2m/s\n$$\n\nLikewise, the velocity is\n\n$$\nv(t) = x'(t) = 6t^2\n$$\n\nso the average acceleration of the particle over the time interval $[0,1]$ is\n\n$$\na_{avg} = \\frac{Δv}{Δt} = (v(1) - v(0))/(1 - 0) = (6(1)^{2} - 6(0)^{2})/(1 - 0) = 6m/s^{2}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "e1c49e4b-7206-5819-b127-c2f562fa1043" :tutorial/math-academy-id 1023 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "defa2861-ea0b-5be8-a72a-4101e1177359" :step/math-academy-id 2011 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097589}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097589 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096717 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096517 :question/id #uuid "924d743e-4984-5d94-84be-381c99697940" :question/math-academy-id "e-571"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7a24f6a-aa0d-576a-a4ff-945335f3301b" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050572} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050901}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097203} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097286}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Velocity of a Particle Given Its Position Function"} :step/id #uuid "c2c3e774-0466-5687-8348-ec20933d1013" :step/math-academy-id 2012 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097590}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097590 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096718 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096521 :question/id #uuid "523927ce-8e24-554d-8558-07f51a3d4120" :question/math-academy-id "e-572"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6d62ff71-fe48-5612-8f37-bab7cb7f2931" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048713}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097285} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097291} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535954} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548039} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548075}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Acceleration of a Particle Given Its Velocity Function"} :step/id #uuid "9c935206-0fc0-512a-9bf5-4f346bee6bcf" :step/math-academy-id 2014 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097591}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097591 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097792 :tutorial/content "So, we now know how to find\n\n- the average *velocity* (given the *position*), and\n- the average *acceleration* (given the *velocity*).\n\nBut what if we are given the *velocity* and asked to find the average *velocity*? That's a bit trickier. However, we can solve this problem by recalling that the average value of a function $v(t)$ over the interval $[t_1,t_2]$ is given by\n\n$$\nv_{\\textrm{avg}} = \\dfrac{1}{t_2-t_1}\\int_{t_1}^{t_2} v(t)\\,\\textrm d t\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "b25ff39d-cfec-5109-8c49-31a8d54ad75d" :tutorial/math-academy-id 1026 :tutorial/title "Calculating Average Velocity Using Integration"} :step/id #uuid "12ea46a3-a7a9-5273-ae68-f843dba89bf3" :step/math-academy-id 2016 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097592}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097592 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096719 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096525 :question/id #uuid "62944da5-875f-542a-9b54-9c3d3c5db947" :question/math-academy-id "e-573"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "803ac4f0-61fe-5efc-b7a5-c73a4235f4bc" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049280}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097293} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097294} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535989} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548076}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Velocity of a Particle Using Integration"} :step/id #uuid "7fa5d198-6f76-58fe-a0de-a2eede2c04f2" :step/math-academy-id 2017 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097676}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097593 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096720 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186096526 :question/id #uuid "aa1e2c54-80dc-5e38-a149-c7db63deb418" :question/math-academy-id "e-574"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3046ebca-8a30-5228-a003-b8155cd1a62a" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097287} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097292} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186527967} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535972} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548036} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548080}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Average Position or Acceleration of a Particle Using Integration"} :step/id #uuid "63d935f4-c3b0-5692-aa00-a8d6bc7db985" :step/math-academy-id 2019} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097676 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097881 :tutorial/content "We can also calculate the average position $x_{\\textrm{avg}}$ and average acceleration $a_{\\textrm{avg}}$ of a particle over an interval $[t_1, t_2]$ using the following formulas:\n\n$$\nx_{avg} = \\frac{1}{t_{2} - t_{1}}\\int_{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}x(t)dt; a_{avg} = \\frac{1}{t_{2} - t_{1}}\\int_{t_{1}}^{t_{2}}a(t)dt\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "8e1cdc1f-de87-5b91-9ad0-f2bcab98be3f" :tutorial/math-academy-id 5192 :tutorial/title "Calculating Average Position and Acceleration Using Integration"} :step/id #uuid "4f5e263b-c885-5894-bec5-5d0237b91689" :step/math-academy-id 32551 :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097593}}] :activity/title "Average Position, Velocity, and Acceleration" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186096868}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536014} :activity/id #uuid "b6659aa2-fce6-56a0-9a42-d00a9aa7628c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048976 :topic/id #uuid "d0827a60-1270-5e75-a5db-1a9836dc00b1" :topic/math-academy-id 1079} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536014 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097292 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04edbe72-2860-5445-9b78-8c22cc20067e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "32\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535444} {:answer/id #uuid "42d18385-9cde-5883-ac5a-37781eda6692" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "31\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535538} {:answer/id #uuid "b4d8c80f-bf74-5759-9834-cd33f9e368f1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{63}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535712} {:answer/id #uuid "e90ae4b7-57a0-56d4-b078-d5b219cd95b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "16\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535795} {:answer/id #uuid "f81b9df8-fff8-5d97-9c34-430dd36b2e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{31}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535814}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535538} :answer-field/id #uuid "e2f77a72-36b9-58bf-9d44-3ce7efb23445" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095676}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "06277fd5-c6be-5879-81ac-2b86cefe4004" :question/math-academy-id "q-50029" :question/problem "A cat’s position relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by the function $x(t)=3{t}^{2}+t$ meters, where $t$ is the time in hours. Find the average position of the cat between $2$ and $4$ hours." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "To calculate the average value of the position on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}\\,{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}x(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{4-2}\\,{\\int }_{2}^{4}(3{t}^{2}+t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{({t}^{3}+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[({4}^{3}+\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2})-({2}^{3}+\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(64+8)-(8+2)] \\\\  & =31.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average position is $31\\,\\text{m}.$"} :step/id #uuid "2ccbe3d6-2634-5637-9466-9ccd96f0e3f1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536015}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536015 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186097294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44246c94-6d8c-5f04-baa0-79045398a988" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "166\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535540} {:answer/id #uuid "7e5d16bc-cb25-52d2-b98e-5bb7f17439e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "160\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535633} {:answer/id #uuid "81eb2493-7567-5c70-bfd8-ceecf2a4addb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "158\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535641} {:answer/id #uuid "b0d18fe2-8169-5eb1-b785-85e842c937f8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "162\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535707} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e9b334-945a-5161-b29a-cb81ea2bb950" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "164\\,\\text{km/h}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535730}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535707} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa9db443-300e-5082-920a-12147e35440b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186095688}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "e6f31648-32f5-5f87-b9bb-fc4d6a7438c9" :question/math-academy-id "q-50036" :question/problem "A train is moving north-east with velocity $v(t)=6{t}^{2}+8t+100\\,\\text{km/h},$ where $t$ is the time in hours. Find the average velocity of the train on the interval $t\\in [1,4].$" :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "To calculate the average value of the velocity on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{v}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{4-1}\\,{\\int }_{1}^{4}(6{t}^{2}+8t+100)\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(2{t}^{3}+4{t}^{2}+100t){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}((2(4)^{3}+4(4)^{2}+100(4))-(2(1)^{3}+4(1)^{2}+100(1))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}((128+64+400)-(2+4+100)) \\\\  & =162.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average velocity is $162\\,\\text{km/h}.$"} :step/id #uuid "33ff57a1-4ad9-5365-8370-762afd29d628" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536042}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536019 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535972 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5859ef23-64ea-5f95-8062-f7664d1b6145" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{14}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535576}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535576} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ab3c0e2-4bdc-50da-b2cf-5a837a9baa2c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535847}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "948c8637-9616-53cf-93bb-0432892cbe59" :question/math-academy-id "q-354500" :question/problem "A particle’s acceleration in ${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$ is given by the function $a(t)=\\sqrt{t},$ where $t$ is the time in seconds.  \n\nFind the average acceleration ${a}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the particle on the interval $[1,4].$ Do not round your answer.\n\n${a}_{\\text{avg}}=$ \n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the average value of the acceleration on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{a}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}a(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{4-1}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{(\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3/2})|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 8)-(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{16}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{14}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{14}{9}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average acceleration is $\\frac{14}{9}\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$"} :step/id #uuid "403b655a-e00c-5598-8326-fcf7ee2d0ed6"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536023 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535989 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "561dec26-edfd-5f06-be74-04ce011e37e6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{32}{9}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535571}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535571} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d89cc03-11cb-5a33-a4d3-defd63d2cbf9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "c00bebe5-d517-59a2-a7ee-fce25fbbc516" :question/math-academy-id "q-354478" :question/problem "A small rover moves along a straight track with velocity \n$v(t)=\\sqrt{t}+2,$ where $t$ is measured in seconds and $v$ is measured in meters per second.\n\nFind the average velocity ${v}_{\\text{avg}}$ on the interval $[1,4].$ Do not round your answer.\n\n${v}_{\\text{avg}}=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$\\text{m/s}$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the average value of the velocity on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{v}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{4-1}{\\int }_{1}^{4}(\\sqrt{t}+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}{(\\frac{2}{3}{t}^{3/2}+2t)|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 8+8)-(\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 1+2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[(\\frac{16}{3}+8)-(\\frac{2}{3}+2)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\frac{40}{3}-\\frac{8}{3}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(\\frac{32}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{32}{9}\\,\\text{m/s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average velocity is $\\frac{32}{9}\\,\\text{m/s}.$"} :step/id #uuid "5ae097ca-dfcf-58c0-b026-e053a35b47c0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536019}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536042 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535954 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12b4a368-f228-50e0-a65e-e556685ce4e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535467}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535467} :answer-field/id #uuid "82e292da-04ee-55d1-86e2-4a2230088d1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "5f1c0a58-fb01-5814-8e30-7c47e655e50c" :question/math-academy-id "q-353938" :question/problem "A robotic rover moves in a straight line with velocity \n$v(t)=3{t}^{2}-t,$ where $t$ is measured in seconds and $v$ is measured in meters per second. \n\nFind the average acceleration ${a}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the rover over the time interval $t\\in [0,2].$ Do not round your answer.\n\n${a}_{\\text{avg}}=$ \n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The average acceleration is the average rate of change of the velocity, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{v(b)-v(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{v(2)-v(0)}{2-0} \\\\  & =\\frac{[3(2)^{2}-2]-[3(0)^{2}-0]}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(12-2)-0}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{2} \\\\  & =5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average acceleration is $5\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$"} :step/id #uuid "c74051f2-6f31-5a23-b00a-9ba4cba0db56" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186536023}}] :activity/title "Average Position, Velocity, and Acceleration" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186535431}] [{:activity/course {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186046645} :activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548142} :activity/id #uuid "214227dc-fd64-5b29-a98a-53e4687a838c" :activity/scope {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048976 :topic/id #uuid "d0827a60-1270-5e75-a5db-1a9836dc00b1" :topic/math-academy-id 1079} :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548101 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548076 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00674e18-ee02-59cd-b3dc-a6f698a1d859" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547317} {:answer/id #uuid "89c053ae-f87b-53b5-b9ff-dddaf3e41c2a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547615} {:answer/id #uuid "8fea7db7-de80-5d17-aee5-ba303c413efc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547636} {:answer/id #uuid "910d3bad-81e3-5314-864f-7990eaa9b236" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547640} {:answer/id #uuid "a5081cba-4b6f-5bf9-b175-aba9c3e125ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{8}\\,\\text{m/s}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547678}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547317} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d349dd1-b5a9-5935-ae21-26e3ea46f260" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "f371caa1-75a3-5280-8f9d-dfa2d56f63d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-83246" :question/problem "A golden eagle is moving in a straight line with a velocity of $v(t)=\\frac{{2}^{t}}{12}\\,\\text{m/s},$ where $t$ is the time in seconds. Find the average velocity of the golden eagle on the interval $[2,6].$" :question/worked-solution "To calculate the average value of the velocity on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{v}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}v(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{v}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{6-2}\\,{\\int }_{2}^{6}(\\frac{{2}^{t}}{12})\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 12\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({2}^{t}){|}_{2}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{48\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}({2}^{6}-{2}^{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{60}{48\\operatorname{ln}⁡2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average velocity is $\\frac{5}{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡2}\\,\\text{m/s}.$"} :step/id #uuid "4de83977-8c26-5f9c-9592-d123404947ae" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548187}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548104 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548039 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63c71e9a-e2a4-5acf-9c3f-1545635639b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547535}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547535} :answer-field/id #uuid "1fb540b7-e7ae-5a07-bd6e-28e04440e173" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547858}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a7420375-7675-57fc-8640-9f218c433ea5" :question/math-academy-id "q-353947" :question/problem "A test cart moves in a straight line with velocity \n$v(t)=\\frac{3}{t},$ where $t$ is measured in seconds and $v$ is measured in feet per second.\n\nFind the average acceleration ${a}_{\\text{avg}}$ over the time interval $t\\in [1,3].$ Do not round your answer.\n\n${a}_{\\text{avg}}=$ \n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{ft/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The average acceleration is the average rate of change of the velocity, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{v(3)-v(1)}{3-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{[\\frac{3}{3}]-[\\frac{3}{1}]}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-3}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{2} \\\\  & =-1\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average acceleration is $-1\\,{\\text{ft/s}}^{2}.$"} :step/id #uuid "52a18bf8-46c8-55cc-86be-84ef4fc0b8e5"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548111 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548075 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37a3d483-228d-5bd2-9d7d-ce2ef8b4ae21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547432}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547432} :answer-field/id #uuid "4686715d-a18c-51be-a9b1-884139acad2f" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547877}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "f05a5b67-91d9-5027-a739-e465c398f589" :question/math-academy-id "q-353941" :question/problem "A robotic sled moves along a straight track with velocity \n$v(t)={t}^{3}-t,$ where $t$ is measured in seconds and $v$ is measured in meters per second.\n\nFind the average acceleration ${a}_{\\text{avg}}$ over the time interval $t\\in [1,3].$ Do not round your answer.\n\n${a}_{\\text{avg}}=$ \n{{field-1}}\n${\\text{m/s}}^{2}$" :question/worked-solution "The average acceleration is the average rate of change of the velocity, so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{v(b)-v(a)}{b-a} \\\\  & =\\frac{v(3)-v(1)}{3-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{[(3)^{3}-(3)]-[(1)^{3}-(1)]}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(27-3)-(1-1)}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24-0}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{2} \\\\  & =12\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average acceleration is $12\\,{\\text{m/s}}^{2}.$"} :step/id #uuid "61e5473c-1f0c-5045-8fdc-52635fbe7581" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548104}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548142 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548080 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d1be747-8a94-5aed-aafa-3f8e379525df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{2-\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547374} {:answer/id #uuid "2bcb7040-6f3f-5555-bdad-85da6ddd1886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547401} {:answer/id #uuid "59823227-e905-5977-a5d2-bb84aa45354b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{8}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547512} {:answer/id #uuid "a6c9df96-aec1-55e9-a6fa-579b1f853ec1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547684} {:answer/id #uuid "e0fc4746-3be8-5122-9467-181003e3756b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\,\\text{m}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547784}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547784} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f66651c-8f9c-52e6-9972-14e6f7d0c2a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547856}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "fbeb0099-1c78-5b43-8e43-b8ec47f11368" :question/math-academy-id "q-50028" :question/problem "A fly’s position relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by the function $x(t)=\\frac{t}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}t)\\,\\text{m},$ where $t$ is the time in minutes. Find its average position of the fly between $0$ and $2$ minutes." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the average value of the position on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}\\,{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}x(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{2-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}(\\frac{t}{2}-\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}t))\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{(\\frac{{t}^{2}}{4}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}t))|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((\\frac{{2}^{2}}{4}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\cdot 2))-(\\frac{{0}^{2}}{4}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}\\cdot 0))) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}((1+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})-(0+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average position is $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{4}\\,\\text{m}.$"} :step/id #uuid "a39df73e-bba8-5942-8e42-4b6f03a5f8e7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548101}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548187 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548036 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "021687c4-7f27-5cfb-bfb5-dc034943da18" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "({e}^{2}+4)\\,{\\text{mm/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547321} {:answer/id #uuid "6afc054d-1902-5c8f-94a1-83ead8f48431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2}-1)\\,{\\text{mm/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547553} {:answer/id #uuid "a0081eee-8909-542d-b183-dcd4d72c126a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "(2e+3)\\,{\\text{mm/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547665} {:answer/id #uuid "db17edff-e21c-5200-a414-f3d057a203d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2}+3)\\,{\\text{mm/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547777} {:answer/id #uuid "ec3107cf-6266-5c72-895b-2d1cbe80c372" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}({e}^{2}+1)\\,{\\text{mm/s}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547806}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186547777} :answer-field/id #uuid "76075077-a9d5-595a-9adb-0f742d7f6853" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "a23536ce-7cba-5974-838f-a84131e7f6d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-83252" :question/problem "Find the average acceleration of a particle on the interval $[0,2]$ if its acceleration in ${\\text{mm/s}}^{2}$ is given by the function $a(t)={e}^{t}+2t,$ where $t$ is the time in seconds." :question/worked-solution "To calculate the average value of the acceleration on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{a}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}\\,{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}a(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{a}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{2-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}({e}^{t}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{t}+{t}^{2}){|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[({e}^{2}+{2}^{2})-({e}^{0}+{0}^{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2}+4-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2}+3).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average acceleration is $\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{2}+3)\\,{\\text{mm/s}}^{2}.$"} :step/id #uuid "fe08ca81-b796-5651-89ae-d412960171ff" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186548111}}] :activity/title "Average Position, Velocity, and Acceleration" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186547294}]}
